Basic Arabic is an important basic course in this profession. Students are mainly taught basic knowledge and basic theories in Arabic, such as voice, vocabulary and grammar, and are strictly guided by the principles of shallow and progressive teaching. They are trained in basic abilities, such as speech, calligraphy, basic vocabulary, sentence and grammar. They are fully equipped with basic skills in listening, speaking, reading and writing and have the initial ability to speak and write in Arabic. Through two years of study, the requirements of the basic Arabic curriculum have been met and a solid foundation has been laid for students to enter the upper grades.
