Electronic lines (linear circuits, analogue circuits) are important basic courses in e-science/electronic engineering.

The mission of the course is to:
1. To enable students to understand and master the theory, methods, of linear circuits;
2. To enable students to understand and master the underlying principles and analytical methods of analog electronic circuits;
3. Awareness of some common basic circuit modules and structures;
4. To enable students to successfully complete courses such as the follow-up electronic circuit experiment.

